Reconstruct the MEMMGR deep block-relocating allocator FUN_1000_0dc2 (0x10dcd..0x10eca) + the exact-
adjacent variant FUN_1000_0ecb (0x10ecb) + the free-list surgery callees FUN_1000_10dc (0x110dc sorted
insert), FUN_1000_1117 (0x11117 insert+coalesce), FUN_1000_0cce (0x10cce split/return-remainder) and
FUN_1000_1019 (0x11019 relocation-notify hook).  Supersedes patch 015's deep-path stub (which logged
"unimplemented follow-on" and fell through the guard tail).

WHAT IT DOES.  When a free-list node's owner-guard flag [es:di+2]&0x50 is CLEAR (the mission-load path;
on the boot pool every node has it SET so 0dc2 always takes the fast guard-tail -- see below), 0dc2 runs
the deep allocator: walk the sorted free list for a hole with base < the node's base and size >= the
node's size; relocate the node's CONTENTS down into the hole (0x1000-paragraph rep-movsw block move ->
mm_block_move()); swap the base/size fields; unlink both the node and the hole node; reinsert each into
the sorted list (10dc plain-insert for the node, 1117 insert+coalesce for the hole); split the leftover
back onto the free list (0cce, popping a paragraph off the descriptor pool at DGROUP:0x16e2); and return
CF=0.  The exact-adjacent case (hole.end == node.base) branches to 0ecb, which grows the hole's base past
the relocated node instead of splitting.  1019 is the per-block relocation-notify hook: if
mask[0x1748+bx] & the owner descriptor's [di+2] flags, it FAR-calls the owner's relocation callback
[di+4] so the owner can fix its pointer to the moved block (uninstalled -> fist_icall_far no-ops, the
faithful non-error path).

MODEL.  SS=DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, BP=0x16d4.  Node paragraph fields: [0]=base seg (sort key) [2]=flags
[4]=size (paragraphs) [6:8]=owner far ptr [0xc]=next-seg [0xe]=prev-seg.  Control frame:
[bp+4]=free-total=MM_ABS16(0x16d8), [bp+0xc]=anchor=MM_ABS16(0x16e0); desc pool head=MM_ABS16(0x16e2),
count=MM_ABS16(0x16dc).  All node/frame accesses go through the patch-025 MM_S16/MM_S8/MM_ABS16 macros
and the shared g_mm_ds/g_mm_es/g_mm_cf/g_mm_zf cursors (DS/ES/CF/ZF are not __allregs-threaded across the
near calls, so these cooperating same-subsystem routines share them explicitly, exactly as patches
015/025 already do for 096c/0a31/0d70/1114).  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin
0x10cce/0x10dc2/0x10ecb/0x110dc/0x11117/0x11019.

BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRALITY (covered flows).  The whole deep chain (0dc2-deep, 0ecb, 10dc, 1117, 0cce, and the
1019 node-cursor read) is reached ONLY on the ACCEPT mission-load cascade: the boot MEMMGR pool nodes all
have [2]&0x50 set, so 0dc2's guard-tail is always taken on the 19 covered flows and these functions are
DEAD there.  PROOF: the Ghidra-mangled bodies this patch replaces deref host address 0 (`*(uint*)0x0`)
and would SIGSEGV at -O0 if executed -- yet all 19 flows are 19/19 and default boot is bit-identical
(mainmenu md5 3a6ff1c5, verified after this patch).  1019 (also called by FUN_1000_0d2e(0xe)) and 0cce
(also called by FUN_1000_18e4/0e8b) stay behaviour-neutral on boot: the mainmenu md5 is unchanged.

RESIDUAL RISK (documented per doctrine -- honest reporting).  The deep relocate mutates the heap on the
ACCEPT cascade, which is NOT yet AE=0, so the block move + list surgery cannot be BIT-verified
render-correct.  It is validated by: (a) the patch-015 "0dc2 ... unimplemented follow-on" warning
VANISHING; (b) NO SIGSEGV in the reconstruction across repeated cascade runs (deep path fires once,
ds=0x39d6, crash-free); (c) the boot MEMMGR invariants + mainmenu bit-identity unchanged; (d) verify.sh
19/19 native<->wasm bit-identical.  The op-0x4c display-list frame loop does NOT yet terminate (the
mission viewport geometry at DGROUP:0x7aa4 is still uninitialised -- the next frontier), but its inbox
range advances (0x26e4..0x2764) and the alloc now completes instead of stalling in the guard tail.

